From: FAN789 <https://github.com/FAN789/luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: hiveton_h5000m: hand PWM fan policy to userspace

Imported verbatim from luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol 2.1.0
(openwrt-patches/h5000m-userspace-fan-control.patch).

The H5000M device tree inherits four cooling maps from mt7987.dtsi.  Three of
them drive the same PWM channel that luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol owns, so the
kernel thermal governor and the userspace controller fight over pwm1.  Drop the
three PWM-owning maps and keep cpu-active-hot, so CPU throttling, the hot trip
and the critical shutdown trip stay in the kernel exactly as before.

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-hiveton-h5000m.dts b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-hiveton-h5000m.dts
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-hiveton-h5000m.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-hiveton-h5000m.dts
@@ -100,3 +100,14 @@
 };
 
+/*
+ * Fan policy is managed by luci-app-h5000m-fancontrol. Keep the CPU cooling,
+ * hot and critical trips intact, but prevent the thermal governor from racing
+ * userspace for the same PWM output.
+ */
+&{/thermal-zones/cpu-thermal/cooling-maps} {
+	/delete-node/ cpu-active-high;
+	/delete-node/ cpu-active-low;
+	/delete-node/ cpu-passive;
+};
+
 &gmac0 {
